@startuml activation
title Companion to M-DP3: activation, maintenance and node-wide operator stop (§§6, 11)
actor "Operator" as A
participant "Phone app\noperator device key; secure element" as P
participant "Terminal\npassword sudo; timestamp_timeout=0" as T
participant "Operator command\nswarma-operator; no harness sessions" as O
participant "Read-only account\nswarma-observer" as R
participant "Dispatcher service\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher" as D
database "Durable state\njournal, effects, claims, maintenance progress" as J
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; exec.stop and absence evidence" as H
participant "Service installer / manager" as I
participant "Credential broker" as B
participant "Session host" as SH
== initial activation, slice 0 ==
I -> O : protected no-harness swarma-operator; broker operator/account owner; helper operator UID
I -> R : mandatory read-only swarma-observer
I -> O : phone path when configured: pinned device key/forced command; terminal password fallback
I -> H : R-RANGE-DENY static UID-range deny before accounts; active precedence probe
I -> D : authenticated/operator-controlled time source; qualified matrix/profile/socket evidence\ninstall/start; admission closed
D -> J : exclusive state; validate compatibility; replay journal
D -> D : valid auth/indexes -> recovery controls reachable
D -> D : classify records; reconcile with unlocked per-record calls
alt unbounded identity/accounting/shared-state uncertainty or global barrier
  D -> D : forward admission closed; authorised controls stay reachable
else complete accounting and unresolved effects confined to retained claims/identities
  D -> D : forward ready for unrelated sound work; uncertain records blocked
end
R -> D : dispatcher state reads; no confirmation
D --> R : status/grants/accounts/bindings as represented; no mutation authority
== node-wide emergency stop (R-ALLSTOP; manual operator act) ==
alt phone path
  A -> P : authenticate and one confirmation of node-wide stop
  P -> O : signed exact act; SSH forced command, no shell
else terminal fallback
  A -> T : password sudo into operator account; no cached ticket
  T -> O : node-wide stop act
end
O -> O : verify act; refuse agent-session origin
alt invalid authentication / confirmation / signature or agent-session origin
  break no node-wide effect
    O --> A : refuse operator act
  end
else operator act admitted
  O -> D : authenticated operator node-wide narrowing act; format unpublished
end
D -> J : journal act; set fail-closed hold before admission
D -> H : separately journaled range deny-all effect
loop every agent/workplace generation and execution
  D -> J : journal current-execution stop intent; unlocked call
  D -> H : exec.stop; account-wide confirmed absence required
  H --> D : absence or unfinished/unknown evidence
  D -> J : persist real result; retain unresolved claims
end
D -> B : separately journaled freeze of all leases and renewals
B --> D : freeze result; delivered tokens keep vendor lifetime
D -> SH : separately journaled close delivery and snapshot bound boards
SH --> D : host result
alt any part partial / refused / unknown
  D -> J : preserve all obligations; admission remains closed
else every part confirmed
  D -> J : stopped; hold stays until explicit recovery
end
opt explicit authenticated operator recovery
  O -> D : explicit recovery act; never automatic restart
  D -> D : require resolved service parts and ordinary readiness before reopening
end
note over D,SH : Each service journals its own part; act/record/recovery formats unpublished.
== bounded maintenance attempt ==
alt main phone path
  A -> P : review exact content (who, actions, until when); biometric confirmation
  P -> P : sign canonical content; device key never leaves phone
  P -> O : SSH over tailnet; device-key-only login; forced command; no shell\nsigned operator record
  O -> O : verify against pinned phone key; signature bound to this act
else terminal fallback (works without phone)
  A -> T : password sudo into swarma-operator; no NOPASSWD; no cached ticket
  T -> O : confirm exact content; signed operator record under operator authority
end
O -> O : refuse agent-session origin; require authentication and content confirmation
O -> D : signed selected-stop maintenance authority under swarma-operator
D -> D : verify operator record and origin/confirmation; refuse agent-session origin before stop
alt agent-session origin / invalid signature / missing authentication or content confirmation
  break no selected stop or maintenance effect
    D --> O : refuse; operator authority required
  end
else signed operator authority admitted
  D -> J : retain signed selected-stop authority
end
note over O,D : Operator command/signature, authorization, deadline/progress and restart-review encoding unpublished (§16).
D -> D : close new admission
D -> J : durable inventory and selected-stop intent
loop selected affected executions from user-manager §7 R-FATE table; bounded deadline
  D -> J : local lock: journal stop + in-flight marker; unlock
  D -> H : exec.stop through dispatcher authority; same E-stop/arguments\ncurrent-execution fence + account-wide scope; no state lock held
  alt stop refused / unknown or process absence unconfirmed
    D -> J : preserve unresolved stop and claim; defer maintenance
  else confirmed no execution process remains
    H --> D : termination receipt
    D -> J : record absence/outcome; reconcile effects/receipts
  end
end
alt deadline exhausted / incomplete reconciliation / any affected process not confirmed absent
  D -> D : defer with admission closed; no mode/schema/binary change
  D --> O : durable progress and unresolved obligations for review/resumption
else all affected executions confirmed absent and reconciled
  D -> J : retain standing allocations and identities; persist intended restarts for review
  D -> I : exclusive state ownership; validate reader/writer compatibility
  I -> I : admitted backend-mode / mutable-state migration / binary swap
  I -> D : start selected compatible service with admission closed
  D -> J : recover/reconcile; retain all later durable records
  alt compatibility / accounting / confinement unresolved or global barrier
    D -> D : remain closed; rollback uses same absence and compatibility fences
  else all records classified and accounting/confined unknowns safe
    D -> D : controls reachable; forward ready for sound records
  end
end
opt operator-reviewed restart
  O -> D : fresh authority and admitted plan/transport
  D -> D : fresh prepare/start checks, including revocation.check
  D -> D : start only admitted rows; unsupported rows remain visibly stopped
end
note over D,J
  Authorised status/observe/reconcile/stop reachable after control prerequisites.
  R-LOCK: cross-service workers hold no state lock; bounded per-record markers.
  F-17: declared restore closes admission before bytes visible; external mark,
  ledger epoch floor, independent coverage and reverse accounts/bindings/receipts inventory.
  Orphans require signed swarma-operator decision via phone or terminal; never from agent sessions.
  No restored snapshot certifies absence; no operator key restore into a harness account.
  Standing re-grants use the same operator path; no automatic delegation published.
  Key enrolment/rotation/phone loss open; terminal re-enrolment proposed (§16).
  R-TIME: trusted watermark max expiry / min not_before; monotonic lifetime for deletion.
  V1 deny-all service-profile row/resolver evidence verified at start/schedule (§13).
  Maintenance deadline bounds the attempt, never standing execution lifetime.
  No standing retirement/identity revocation, automatic expiry or live adoption.
  Queue drain alone never stops executions. No snapshot rollback repair.
  Native resume is gated by §12; no seamless continuation is promised.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#11-installation-and-activation §11 activation/maintenance]] / §§7, 8.1, 16
endlegend
@enduml
